<ns0:section xmlns:ns0="http://xml.house.gov/schemas/uslm/1.0" style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="id990dc3f1-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc" identifier="/us/usc/t42/s1997d"><ns0:num value="1997d">§ 1997d.</ns0:num><ns0:heading> Prohibition of retaliation</ns0:heading><ns0:content>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">No person reporting conditions which may constitute a violation under this subchapter shall be subjected to retaliation in any manner for so reporting.</ns0:p>
</ns0:content><ns0:sourceCredit id="id990dc3f2-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc">(<ns0:ref href="/us/pl/96/247/s6">Pub. L. 96–247, § 6</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1980-05-23">May 23, 1980</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/94/352">94 Stat. 352</ns0:ref>.)</ns0:sourceCredit>
</ns0:section>
